f916d50f54d540378f3eba684293fe7edf3a913015ab9f7da21c881b6ea69","file":"preprints/Milnes-rationality-conjecture-for-abelian-varieties-October-7-2026/build/sections/00_intro.tex","line":29,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"7dc9abdf7cbc67fd670f2d4ef4eef85d4c2a77ca3a255c14915ff7205916eb8a","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Milnes-rationality-conjecture-for-abelian-varieties-October-7-2026/build/sections/00_intro.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:848f916d50f54d540378f3eba684293fe7edf3a913015ab9f7da21c881b6ea69","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Milnes-rationality-conjecture-for-abelian-varieties-October-7-2026/build/sections/00_intro.tex#L29"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet \\(A/\\Qbar\\) be an abelian variety of dimension \\(d\\) with good\nreduction \\(A_0/\\F\\) at \\(w\\). Let \\(0\\leq r\\leq d\\), and let\n\\[\n \\gamma\\in H^{2r}(A(\\C),\\Q(r))\n\\]\nbe a rational Hodge class. For every list of Cartier divisors\n\\(D_1,\\ldots,D_{d-r}\\) on \\(A_0\\), there is a number \\(q\\in\\Q\\)\nsuch that\n\\begin{align*}\n \\Tr_\\ell\\bigl(\\gamma_{0,\\ell}\n       c_{1,\\ell}(D_1)\\cdots c_{1,\\ell}(D_{d-r})\\bigr)&=q\n       &&\\text{in }\\Q_\\ell\\quad(\\ell\\ne p),\\\\\n \\Tr_p\\bigl(\\gamma_{0,p}\n       c_{1,\\mathrm{cris}}(D_1)\\cdots\n       c_{1,\\mathrm{cris}}(D_{d-r})\\bigr)&=q\n       &&\\text{in }\\Cw.\n\\end{align*}\nHere \\(\\gamma_{0,\\ell}\\) is the smooth proper specialization of the\n\\(\\ell\\)-adic realization, and \\(\\gamma_{0,p}\\) is the\nde Rham--crystalline specialization in\n\\[\n H^{2r}_{\\mathrm{cris}}(A_0/W(\\F))[1/p](r)\n       \\otimes_{\\Kzero}\\Cw.\n\\]\nThe traces use the top Tate twist and send the class of a zero-cycle to\nits degree. If \\(r=d\\), the divisor product is \\(1\\)."}
